    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'10'03PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 03.10.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2143$47 - 2019 Tlaf;dan\u00be ui 03 jeks n%yiam;skaod - 2019'10'03No. 2143/47 - THURSDAY, OCTOBER 03, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk1A - PG 4670\u2014 517 (10/2019)\n\nORDERS ISSUED BY THE ELECTION COMMISSION IN ADDITION TO THOSE PREVIOUSLYISSUED BY THE ELECTION COMMISSION BY GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY No. 2141/52 DATED19TH SEPTEMBER 2019\n\nWHEN the Election Commission decides that it is necessary to inquire further into the information or complaints receivedby it regarding the violation of an order or orders issued by the Election Commission to prevent the misuse of governmentproperty in connection with the election and orders to submit relevant print or electronic documents, discussion notes,reports including those relating to the recruitment or appointment, to the Election Commission or of an officer authorizedby the Election Commission, public officers in charge of such documents should take action to provide all relevantinformation. In such instances when the Election Commission or an officer authorized by the Election Commissionorders to submit any oral or written statement for further inquiries into an incident where any order or orders issued bythe Election Commission have been violated, relevant public officers should be responsible for providing all-inclusivestatements. They are bound to do so."
