    "chunk_text": "d) foster public procurement planning, in order to timely integrate GPP and SPP criteria in to the Procurement Process;\n\ne) first starting strategy of GPP is to begin with commonly use Goods, Works and Services\n\nand to expand the green procurement list;\n\n15.4 Role play by the Ministry of EnvironmentRefer\n\nManual15.4The Ministry in charge of the subject of environment shall establish an Inter-Agency Expert Committee on Green Public Procurement. (IAEC- GPP).\n\n15.5 Introducing Green Specifications for Commonly Used ItemsRefer\n\nManual15.5IAEC may develop green specifications for commonly used products, Goods and Works using existing certified material by local green certification organizations. Each PE shall obtain approval for their green specifications from IAEC.\n\n15.6 Inclusion of Green Public Procurement criteria in Procurement Documents Refer\n\nManual15.6For the purchase of common use items, each PE may be adopted green specifications as \u201cmandatory\u201d features in the bid/proposal specifications when the products are available on the market with adequate models and quantities in supply. In this connection, \u201cmandatory\u201d green requirements are specified in the Manual.\n\nFor new green specifications developed with uncertain market availability, green specifications will be included in the bid/proposal specifications as \u201cdesirable\u201d features. \u201cDesirable\u201d green requirements are also specified in the Manual."
